Subject: [PATCH] hw/gpio: bound per-transaction resolver work

Keep the existing GPIO/pad/IRQ data plane and ordering. Avoid unused private
timestamps and unrelated pin resolution, sample each before/commit phase once,
and reuse only stable same-transaction snapshots. Limit bank writes to active
S3 word accesses; selected legacy listeners and level IRQs retain the full path.
Synchronous newly registered listeners still receive real callbacks and fresh
post-callback IRQ state. Public snapshot timestamps intentionally describe one
transaction phase rather than host pin-iteration skew.

Original GPIO GPL-2.0-or-later header is retained unchanged.

diff --git a/hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c b/hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c
index edd81dc..3f7c52a 100644
